Z||000000||mrfixit58||11-20-2001||07:50 PM||||Well, maybe not THE holy grail but darned close! It's the car I've been after for almost three years. A 1988 Yellow GT, CJB coded T-Top car with 5-speed and a performance sound system. Number 89 of all 1988s T-tops built. The pictures aren't that great but all I have right now. What do you guys think?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front_11.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rear.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/option_codes.jpg"> <P>It has 91k miles and runs great. The previous owner kept impeccable maintenance records and always kept the car on a carport. It needs a little scrubbing, axles seals, and some new dew wipes but little else. It's not perfect but it's all original and very nice.<P>Just thought I'd share,<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||10
