Z||000027||artherd||11-21-2001||11:10 PM||||There's something about those CBJs, eh?<P>Great car!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000028||FieroJoe||11-21-2001||11:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 4UMLA1:<BR><B>What does CJB mean, and why is it such a special Fiero?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yellow, T-Top 88 GT's are one of the smallest part of the Fiero population.  88's are very nice to have to begin with, but yellow, and with factory T-tops, are very hard to come by.<P>The CBJ vehicle build code represents that this car came out of the factory with the C&C t-tops installed.  You can find Fieros, both 88 (only year t-tops offered) and non 88 with the factory type T-tops (C&C).  In 1988, when t-tops were offerend on Fieros out of the factory, dealers were also allowed to install the factory style t-tops on previously sold Fieros.  CBJ would not appear on cars with dealer installed t-tops.  <P>Oh, and if you don't know what we're talking about with the build codes, a sheet is affixed to the left front wheel well in the front trunk compartment, with a list of 3 character codes that tell what is on your Fiero from the factory.||||reg||1
Z||000029||SKIDMARK||11-22-2001||01:19 AM||||There was a guy in PA last summer selling a pair, 88 GT and 88 Formula, both yellow and both with less than 20K on them. I don't remember if they were T top or not. He was asking some real big bucks. Made me appreciate the yellow Fieros more. <BR>Really sharp car, glad to see it go to someone who'll take care of it.||||reg||1
